//! Draws a finished `ui_scene.Scene` with WebGPU, natively through Dawn and in the browser.
//!
//! Each batch of the scene is one instanced draw: quads (rounded-rectangle SDF with borders and
//! dashes), shadows (closed-form Gaussian along x, sampled along y), underlines, monochrome
//! sprites with text gamma and contrast correction, polychrome sprites, and path coverage strips.
//! All instances of a frame live in persistent storage buffers, one per kind, that grow when a
//! frame outgrows them and are never shrunk.
//!
//! A scene without isolated layers draws straight onto the target, in one pass.
//!
//! A plain isolated layer (normal blend and no filters: an opacity, a transform, a mask layer)
//! costs no pass of its own. Plain layers of one nesting depth that do not overlap share a
//! target-sized texture, a page, drawn in one pass before their parents, deepest first; the
//! parent's pass then blits each one where it comes in its batches. A mask layer is one more
//! layer, on another page.
//!
//! Every other layer (blend modes, blur, color filters, drop shadows, backdrop blur) is drawn
//! into a texture of its own and composited with gpu_scene's blend modes in a pass that
//! interrupts its parent's, which costs target-sized passes for each. When the root holds such a
//! layer, the frame is drawn into an RGBA8 texture and copied to the target at the end. Textures
//! are pooled across frames.
//!
//! The output is premultiplied, blended in the target's (sRGB-encoded) space, like the CPU
//! reference `ui_scene.cpu.CpuRenderer`, which it matches within a small tolerance rather than byte
//! for byte: analytic SDF edges and the erf blur differ from exact area coverage and a separable
//! Gaussian by a few levels at edges.
